  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/zipball/nightly",
  "body": "## Automated Nightly Builds\n\nThis release contains nightly binary tarballs of Apache Cassandra\ndevelopment branches and tracked forks, each built with its correct\nper-version JDK by the reusable `build-cassandra-ref.yml` engine.\nMatching GHCR container images are published under the moving\n`:cassandra-<ref>` tag.\n\n- **5.0-HEAD**: Latest from `cassandra-5.0` branch (apache/cassandra)\n- **6.0-HEAD**: Latest from `cassandra-6.0` branch (apache/cassandra)\n- **trunk**: Latest from `trunk` branch (apache/cassandra)\n- **6.0-rustyrazorblade-HEAD**: Latest from `cassandra-6.0-rustyrazorblade` branch (rustyrazorblade/cassandra fork)\n- **5.0-rustyrazorblade-HEAD**: Latest from `cassandra-5.0-rustyrazorblade` branch (rustyrazorblade/cassandra fork)\n\n### Stable Download URLs\n\nThese URLs always point to the latest nightly builds:\n\n```\nhttps://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/releases/download/nightly/apache-cassandra-5.0-HEAD-bin.tar.gz\nhttps://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/releases/download/nightly/apache-cassandra-6.0-HEAD-bin.tar.gz\nhttps://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/releases/download/nightly/apache-cassandra-trunk-bin.tar.gz\nhttps://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/releases/download/nightly/apache-cassandra-6.0-rustyrazorblade-HEAD-bin.tar.gz\nhttps://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/releases/download/nightly/apache-cassandra-5.0-rustyrazorblade-HEAD-bin.tar.gz\n```\n\n### Build Information\n\n- **Workflow Run**: https://github.com/rustyrazorblade/cassandra-builds/actions/runs/43835606063\n- **Build Command**: `ant artifacts -Dno-checkstyle=true -Dant.gen-doc.skip=true`\n\n### Usage\n\nThese artifacts are compatible with the `easy-db-lab` Packer build\nsystem and can be used as drop-in replacements for building\nCassandra from source. Per-build (non-moving) releases are also\ncreated for every individual build — see the repo's other\nreleases for a pinned SHA rather than the latest nightly.\n\n---\n\n**Note**: These are development builds and should not be used in production.\n"
